# XSH fclose()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.fclose.001
anchor     functions/fclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       With "hello" buffered in an output stream, fclose() returns 0 and the
           file holds "hello".
test       t/001-flushes.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.002
anchor     functions/fclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       After fclose() of a stream, its descriptor (from fileno()) is no longer
           open.
test       t/002-closes-fd.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.003
anchor     functions/fclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       For a file "0123456789" read through a stream (the active handle) with
           one fgetc(), after fclose() a duplicate of the descriptor taken
           before the call has offset 1.
test       t/003-input-offset.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.004
anchor     functions/fclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       With data buffered in an output stream and the file's times set to
           2001-09-09, after fclose() st_mtim is later than that and st_ctim
           later than before the call.
test       t/004-times.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.005
anchor     functions/fclose.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       With data buffered in a stream whose descriptor was closed,
           fclose() returns EOF with errno EBADF.
test       t/005-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.006
anchor     functions/fclose.html#ERRORS/EPIPE
class      required
since      2001
says       With SIGPIPE blocked and data buffered in a stream on a pipe whose read
           end is closed, fclose() returns EOF with errno EPIPE, and SIGPIPE
           is pending.
test       t/006-epipe.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.007
anchor     functions/fclose.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       When fclose() of a stream on a pipe with no reader fails (EPIPE), the
           stream's descriptor is closed all the same.
test       t/007-closed-on-error.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.008
anchor     functions/fclose.html#ERRORS/EINTR
class      required
since      2001
says       With a stream on a full pipe (blocking) holding 1000 buffered bytes,
           a SIGALRM caught without SA_RESTART 200 ms into fclose() makes it
           return EOF with errno EINTR.
timeout    20
test       t/008-eintr.c

assertion  XSH.fclose.009
anchor     functions/fclose.html#ERRORS/EAGAIN
class      required
since      2001
says       With a pipe filled to capacity and O_NONBLOCK set on its write
           end, fclose() of a stream on that end holding 1000 buffered bytes
           returns EOF with errno EAGAIN.
test       t/009-eagain.c
